<p><em>The Passion Gospel is announced in the following manner</em></p>

<p>The Passion of our Lord Jesus Christ according to __________.</p>

<p><em>The customary reponses before and after the Gospel are omitted.</em></p>

<p>
<em>Year A</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;    <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Matthew 26:36-27:54(55-66)">Matthew 26:36-27:54(55-66)</a>   <em>or</em> <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Matthew 27:1-54(55-66)">27:1-54(55-66)</a><br>

<em>Year B</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;    <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Mark 14:32-15:39(40-47)">Mark 14:32-15:39(40-47)</a>   <em>or</em> <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Mark 15:1-39(40-47)">15:1-39(40-47)</a> <br>

<em>Year C</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;    <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Luke 22:39-23:49(50-56)">Luke 22:39-23:49(50-56)</a>   <em>or</em> <a target=_blank href="<?php echo SERVER;?>#/search/display/Luke 23:1-49(50-56)">23:1-49(50-56)</a> </p>

<p><em>The Passion Gospel may be read or chanted by different persons.
Specific roles may be assigned to different persons, the congregation
taking the part of the crowd.</em></p>

<p><em>The congregation may be seated for the first part of the Passion.  At
the verse which mentions the arrival at Golgotha (Matthew 27:33,
Mark 15:22, Luke 23:33) all stand.</em></p>

<p><em>When the Liturgy of the Palms has preceded, the Nicene Creed and the
Confession of Sin may be omitted at this service.</em></p>

